==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Ice Queen Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ice Crystal Cat''' at level 30 by using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
In early-game, Ice Cat shines in levels with an abundance of short-medium range [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies. Since her attack cooldown, attack rate, range and proc chance for Freeze aren't ideal for absolute crowd control, it is not recommended to use this unit prior to her True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Like most Dynamites, Ice Crystal Cat improves dramatically, as she gains 100 more range and a 100% freeze, granting her consistent uptime. Outside of event enemies, Ice Crystal Cat now finds even greater use in controlling longer-ranged Reds, such as [[Capy]], [[Red EnerG]], and [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]]. She also fares better against enemies that she outranged in her previous forms, having more room to react when they suddenly resume in pushing.

==='''Talents'''===
Ice Crystal Cat's Talents aren't very special and are overall terrible in quality, so there's no reason spending NP on her.

As a high-ranged CC unit with low stats, Ice Crystal Cat could make a little use of '''[[Survive]]'''. '''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' and '''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Slow Resist]]''' are likewise useless, since Ice Crystal Cat cannot handle such enemies at all, and there are better alternatives anyways. Stat Talents are also quite useless unless you are investing in the Strenghten Ultra Talent, in which it is worth considering '''Attack Buff'''.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Ice Crystal Cat's Ultra Talents are very good, transforming her into a viable generalist DPS unit. '''[[Strengthen]]''' is the main selling point. Despite its heavy investment, when maxed and combined with Attack Buff, Ice Crystal Cat can achieve about 23k DPS at Lv.60, which is higher than [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Lord Gao]] at equal levels. Combined with her godly mobility at only 3000 cost and roughly 1 minute cool down, this makes her a very powerful generalist. It is still ill-advised to invest precious [[Catseye|Dark Catseyes]] and NP into her Ultra Talents solely for this damage boost. Her other Talents are decent at best, with '''[[Dodge Attack]]''' being completely unreliable for what it asks for, since said ability only consistently works on highly disposable meatshields or tanks. '''Target Metal''' is a bit better, since Ice Crystal Cat is known for her good uptime and can comfortably outrange them. However, competent anti-Metals are available in spades, and most of them can get the job done regardless of her involvement.

